Important Java 8 features
-------------------------------

Lambda Expressions, Functional Interfaces, static and default methods in Interfaces, Stream API, Date API,
Optional Class, Method references

Lambda Expressions
----------------

LE are the speacial type of functions without any name, access modifier & with no return type written using lambda symbol
->  used to reduce boiler plate code in Java and make code more readable and maintainable

These can be used to provide implementation for Functional Interfaces.

Example: (a,b) -> System.out.println(a+b);

Functional Interfaces
-----------------------

The interface with only one abstract method and they can have many static and default methods

Example for Built in FI - Comparator (with only one abs method - compare()) & Runnable (with only one abs method - run())

We use @FunctionalInterface annotation to denote that the interface is a FI to avoid any compile time checking and restrict
the interface to have only one abstract method.

We can have our own functional interface - User defined - However the rule is to have only one abstract method and they
can have many static and default methods

The instances of functional interfaces can be created with lambda expressions, method references, or constructor references.

